# reference.in: this family's reference requirements, resolved to the exact, hashed reference.lock
# beside this file by `python -m rcp_ndcg_test.jobs.reference_lock` (owner decision 35). The tool
# constrains torch and the CUDA stack to the engine image's freeze; every other pin installs into
# the family's reference venv and takes precedence over the image's copy. Never edit the lock by hand.
# The zerank family's reference environment (one file for all three sizes, decision 34), in ITS
# OWN python (never the harness's process, never the engine image). Install with the reference
# python: pip install -r reference.lock. The wave runner takes it via
# --reference-python; the reference subprocess runs while the engine on that slot is up and
# releases its memory when it exits.
#
# The pins are the paper reference's (experiments/paper/rerankers/reference/requirements.txt, the
# package's former [local] extra): the paper-exact zerank reference runs on torch 2.9.1 +
# transformers 4.57.6. That file's flash-attn and accelerate pins are dropped here: the family's
# reference.py (the paper's ZerankRerank) imports neither. Stage 1 (--mode render) needs only
# tokenizers + huggingface_hub (both are transformers' own dependencies). Stage 2 (--mode score)
# needs torch and the checkpoint weights. The paper's zerank reference computes its sigmoid with
# scipy.special.expit (a hand-rolled math.exp would overflow on very negative logits); the score
# head runs in bf16.

torch>=2.9  # the paper pinned 2.9.1; the family's reference.py imports no flash-attn and runs on the image's torch (decision 35)
transformers==4.57.6
scipy>=1.11
tokenizers>=0.21
huggingface_hub>=0.30,<1.0  # transformers 4.57.6 requires <1.0 (the image ships 1.33.0)
